{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions","id":14823,"title":"Random Demon Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-20T12:18:10-08:00","id":14823,"title":"Random Demon Questions","content":"Where is the xp table? How much xp does a dot of Cover cost?<br /> <br /> With the right combination of options, the Bolthole merit could be the key from <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lost_Room\" target=\"_blank\">the Lost Room.</a> I assume this was intentional?<br /> <br /> If I make a Pact with someone, I end up having the same context to a piece of traded life that they had, right? So, I can't make a pact with a rock star to take the place of their manager, I'd have to make a pact with the manager?<br /> <br /> If I make a Soul Pact which grants the subject a lot of money and then call it in immediately, do I get the money? Do I need to use Legend to get it?<br /> <br /> Can I make a Pact for someone's job? If so, what level is it?<br /> <br /> Is relationship strength objective or subjective? I mean, if a married couple has gone through rough times to the point that they're practically strangers, is it still worth three points? Conversely, if someone is a shy recluse and their only real moment of human contact in a given day is exchanging pleasantries with the pretty barista at the coffee shop they go to every morning and the recluse values that relationship very highly, does it still count as an acquaintanceship (because the barista would certainly consider it such)?<br /> <br /> If I start building a patchwork Cover out of a whole bunch of little relationships and things, do I get to specify the Cover's appearance? Do I ever gain free merits for having a high Cover rating?<br /> <br /> Possibly I just missed this bit, but where are the benefits of having a high Cover described? As it gets more and more embedded into reality, do you gain some of the social benefits of your new life or do you still have to use Legend or XP to get them? If you don't get the social benefits, does reality at least start treating your Cover as more real, with varied clothing and a house that makes physical sense? Is there a table that describes that anywhere?<br /> <br /> If you have multiple Covers, how much time do you need to put into each one before they start degrading? Or does it depend on the Cover? I mean, one assumes that a serial killer can probably go for a long time between killings without much degradation, but an office worker who doesn't turn up for a week is probably going to find their cover wearing dangerously thin. Is that right or did I miss a table somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T17:23:06-08:00","id":14995,"title":"","content":"Piggybacking on this thread:<br /> <br /> Is the Essence Drain demonic form power assumed by default to work on ghosts and spirits (and Astral entities, in the event of Rip the Gates)? The description says angels and demons but specifies that its working on supernaturals not fueled by Essence or Aether is up to the ST, and the power in general seems to be the demonic equivalent of Essence Thief, so I wasn't sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  accidentally a phrase 11-20-2013, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T17:46:12-08:00","id":15008,"title":"","content":"I was gonna post a big ol' list of questions myself, but this hits most of them. I'm particularly interested in the OP's last question, as otherwise it seems that multiple covers demand that all but one has a tenuous connection to society at best.<br /> <br /> To add:<br /> <br /> -Is a Pact capable of stripping more general Merits from a mortal into a Demon's Cover? Close relationships could qualify for Ally or True Friend... but it seems that something like trading a rock star's fanbase (Fame) for curing the cancer brought on by a life of smoking everything they could stick in their mouth and light up - which strikes me as a very Demon-y sort of pact - isn't supported by the rules on either end (since I can't think of a Merit that covers 'lacks a case of cancer', either).<br /> <br /> -Do the Contracts that govern Pacts admit the use of terms external to the agreement, and do they affect the Pact? Does the 'equivalent exchange' system governing pacts care if the demon demands the mortal remit 10% of their new ridiculously boosted income to the demon, will that change the cost of the Pact, and would there be any means of supernatural enforcement applied?<br /> Or was that sort of thing intentionally avoided to keep Pacts from overlapping too much with Changeling Pledges?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 11-20-2013, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T18:36:09-08:00","id":15034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=14995#post14995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Piggybacking on this thread:<br /> <br /> Is the Essence Drain demonic form power assumed by default to work on ghosts and spirits (and Astral entities, in the event of Rip the Gates)? The description says angels and demons but specifies that its working on supernaturals not fueled by Essence or Aether, and the power in general seems to be the demonic equivalent of Essence Thief, so I wasn't sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>By default its presumed to work on Angels and other Demons. It basically says at the end of the powers description that its up the ST if it affects other beings. So if you want Demons to be able to drain essense from Ghosts, Spirits and anything else that has an Essence score you can have it do so (so long as your the ST obviously). If its your game you could have it drain Glamour or Pyros if you wanted. Its entirely in the ST's hands. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd limit it to Demons and Angels, but that's purely my own sensibilities and an attempt to fit the power in with my &quot;taste&quot;. Its by no means a rule or anything though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T19:23:18-08:00","id":15055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions#post14823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is the xp table? How much xp does a dot of Cover cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Three. This will be clearer in the final book; the general Experience cost table is in the Character Creation Quick Reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions#post14823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I make a Pact with someone, I end up having the same context to a piece of traded life that they had, right? So, I can't make a pact with a rock star to take the place of their manager, I'd have to make a pact with the manager?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions#post14823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I make a Soul Pact which grants the subject a lot of money and then call it in immediately, do I get the money?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the money goes where you directed it, which wasn't to yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions#post14823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I make a Pact for someone's job? If so, what level is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can. It's medial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions#post14823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is relationship strength objective or subjective? I mean, if a married couple has gone through rough times to the point that they're practically strangers, is it still worth three points? Conversely, if someone is a shy recluse and their only real moment of human contact in a given day is exchanging pleasantries with the pretty barista at the coffee shop they go to every morning and the recluse values that relationship very highly, does it still count as an acquaintanceship (because the barista would certainly consider it such)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how it matters to the pactee. EDIT: But &quot;matters&quot; doesn't mean &quot;likes.&quot; An estranged wife is likely a major part of the pactee's life, even if her role is &quot;I don't understand her and I don't want to be around her.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions#post14823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I start building a patchwork Cover out of a whole bunch of little relationships and things, do I get to specify the Cover's appearance? Do I ever gain free merits for having a high Cover rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>In character, a patchwork cover accretes elements of the appearances of the people it was made from. Out of character, I'd simply allow the player to select the appearance, and encourage them to incorporate a memorable trait or two from one of the pactees. You never get free Merits from Cover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions#post14823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly I just missed this bit, but where are the benefits of having a high Cover described? As it gets more and more embedded into reality, do you gain some of the social benefits of your new life or do you still have to use Legend or XP to get them? If you don't get the social benefits, does reality at least start treating your Cover as more real, with varied clothing and a house that makes physical sense? Is there a table that describes that anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no table, just the general descriptions of high and low cover. More detail will be provided on this in the <i>Player's Guide</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And of course the mechanical benefits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions#post14823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have multiple Covers, how much time do you need to put into each one before they start degrading? Or does it depend on the Cover? I mean, one assumes that a serial killer can probably go for a long time between killings without much degradation, but an office worker who doesn't turn up for a week is probably going to find their cover wearing dangerously thin. Is that right or did I miss a table somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to spend time in a Cover to keep it from degrading, but if you made a pact for someone's office job, you need to show up for it or you'll probably get fired. Getting fired, though, doesn't affect your cover rating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15008#post15008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Is a Pact capable of stripping more general Merits from a mortal into a Demon's Cover? Close relationships could qualify for Ally or True Friend... but it seems that something like trading a rock star's fanbase (Fame) for curing the cancer brought on by a life of smoking everything they could stick in their mouth and light up - which strikes me as a very Demon-y sort of pact - isn't supported by the rules on either end (since I can't think of a Merit that covers 'lacks a case of cancer', either).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow taking a Merit as part of a pact. I'd treat taking the cancer as a medial benefit. Honestly, you're right, there isn't a good Merit for &quot;lacks life-threatening illness,&quot; so I'd just try to figure out how big a benefit it is for the mortal and put it in one of the three classes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15008#post15008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Contracts that govern Pacts admit the use of terms external to the agreement, and do they affect the Pact? Does the 'equivalent exchange' system governing pacts care if the demon demands the mortal remit 10% of their new ridiculously boosted income to the demon, will that change the cost of the Pact, and would there be any means of supernatural enforcement applied?<br /> Or was that sort of thing intentionally avoided to keep Pacts from overlapping too much with Changeling Pledges?</div> </div> </div> </div>A demon can't make a pact which supernaturally forces a person to hand over a portion of their income. Pacts can only take aspects of lives from people or give things to them by editing reality. They're not general purpose mystical-legal deals.<br /> <br /> Hope these help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 11-20-2013, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T19:26:27-08:00","id":15057,"title":"","content":"As I understand Cover can only be bought with Cover Experience, and one Cover is 3 points.<br /> <br /> If you want to be the manager, you would have to make a pact with the manager. That is his life and thus he has title to it.<br /> <br /> Any Merits dealing with the external nature of the Cover, like Resources or even Striking Looks should be retained. No, you shouldn't need Legend, although that may be needed to mimic the subjects original natural talents like Expression or such.<br /> <br /> Jobs are typically major components to people's life, so I would say three, maybe in two in some cases.<br /> <br /> Relationship strength should be objective. Your wife is a major aspect of your life, even if you hate the bitch. Maybe especially so.<br /> <br /> You get to pick appearance, but no free Merits.<br /> <br /> Higher Covers grant bonuses to compromise checks, and generally degrade slower.<br /> <br /> Time needed varies by Cover.<br /> <br /> You should be able to affect anyone with an Essence score at base. It's cats that don't have an Essence or Aether score that the effect is up in the air. So ghosts and spirits are fair game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T20:15:17-08:00","id":15077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15055#post15055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Three. This will be clearer in the final book; the general Experience cost table is in the Character Creation Quick Reference.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, the money goes where you directed it, which wasn't to yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there intended to be a sort of fuzzy idea of a point at which an external merit granted in a Soul Pact becomes 'owned' by the target and is thus harvestable into the cover based on them? Or is 'don't sell someone something you'll need' part of the idea of Soul Pact crafting, instead reserving rewards for the clever demon who sells a mark abilities that will make them predisposed to acquire what the demon wants in their eventual cover?<br /> <br /> ...I actually find myself rather favoring the second option now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15055#post15055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to spend time in a Cover to keep it from degrading, but if you made a pact for someone's office job, you need to show up for it or you'll probably get fired. Getting fired, though, doesn't affect your cover rating.!</div> </div> </div> </div>For clarity: Does this confirm that if a Cover (or !God help the Demon, multiple covers) has a full-time job or other heavily time-obligated situation, the Cover is required to fully act that out and the partial stasis of not being the active cover only applies to internal aspects? So a Cover with, say, a job as an ER doctor can't feasibly share a Demon with a police officer or cubicle farmer? (Or at least, not remain all of them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15055#post15055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd allow taking a Merit as part of a pact. I'd treat taking the cancer as a medial benefit. Honestly, you're right, there isn't a good Merit for &quot;lacks life-threatening illness,&quot; so I'd just try to figure out how big a benefit it is for the mortal and put it in one of the three classes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A demon can't make a pact which supernaturally forces a person to hand over a portion of their income. Pacts can only take aspects of lives from people or give things to them by editing reality. They're not general purpose mystical-legal deals.<br /> <br /> Hope these help!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds legit. Having extraneous, non-supernaturally-enforced terms in the document carrying the pact doesn't interfere with it, though? Or does the mystical machinery the demon uses to quick-author a pact get cranky like my home network printer when a demon tries to pull that?<br /> <br /> Thanks for popping in to answer, by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T20:27:57-08:00","id":15084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15055#post15055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the money goes where you directed it, which wasn't to yourself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But, since it's a Soul Pact, the target gets the money, which happens immediately, and then I call it in, taking the target's life as my Cover. Doesn't that mean I get the money? Or, at least the lifestyle benefits of the wealth increase, since, iirc, Pacts don't normally grant merits to the demon?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T20:46:24-08:00","id":15096,"title":"","content":"Also, If I can grab someone's job via a Pact, who notices? Just the direct superior? How about coworkers? Clients? If I patch it into a level 9 Cover to boost it to level 10, do more people treat me as having worked there for awhile than if I was weaving it into a level 1 Cover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T21:13:59-08:00","id":15104,"title":"","content":"A Soul Pact should grant any external Merits. You steal the soul of a rich guy, then you are rich. How he got the money, legitimately or otherwise, is irrelevant. The main thing is that you could not immediately collect on a deal like a soul pact for wealth; you would need to wait until the money was accrued and possible until it was cemented as a pat of their persona before you could collect the soul and reap the benefit yourself. Yes this gives you free access to certain merits with a Soul Pact, but 1) It's not protected by Sanctity of Merits and thus is easy come easy go, 2) High external merits tend to draw unwanted attention, and 3) it costs a Willpower <b>dot</b> to close the deal, so I think that's adequate compensation.<br /> <br /> A Job would be everyone directly affected. So your immediate supervisor, immediate coworkers in your department, and regular clients. Other departments, irregular clients, your boss's boss, and the government wouldn't be affected.<br /> <br /> As far as extra-contractual terms and agreements, a Pact doesn't carry any supernatural enforcement power, but can still be implemented, just like getting to signature through threat of force, which is kosher I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T21:54:47-08:00","id":15122,"title":"","content":"&quot;Pacts can only take aspects of lives from people or give things to them by editing reality. They're not general purpose mystical-legal deals.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thanks @Rose. This has cleared up a lot of the questions I've had about pacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:02:45-08:00","id":15125,"title":"","content":"Yeah, getting a signature via threat of force is perfectly legit. &quot;Sign this or I will murder your family&quot;, while probably grossly out of character for your Cover, is a legitimate way of getting a signature on a contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:26:23-08:00","id":15135,"title":"","content":"Couple of questions about angels, if you don't mind.<br /> <br /> 1) The text under Aetheric Resonance says that angels don't have any counterpart for flushing out the Unchained. However, under Aetheric Sense in the Cryptid section it says that it's what Angels use to track down demons. Which is correct?<br /> <br /> 2) Related to the above, the text says that a demon who goes out into the wilderness is a prime target for the God-Machine, which is why they stay in the cities. How do angels threaten these hermetic Unchained? Even if they have the Aetheric Sense mentioned above, how do they get the angels out there without the Infrastructure as a refueling station and a staging ground, either via possession or materialization? Is it just that the God-Machine eventually tracks them down via plot device and sends out Rank 4+ angels that can create Infrastructure? Because that'd be pretty bad for lone demons.<br /> <br /> 3) Speaking of Infrastructure and possession, how exactly does that work? Are mortals taken to Facilities and turned into &quot;Infrastructure&quot; via brainwashing, modification, etc like sleeper agents? Or does the nature of the Infrastructure envelop the people inside of it, allowing angels to take possession of those who are currently standing in Infrastructure?<br /> <br /> 4) I don't see anything in the text saying that angels must look nonhuman, and the fact that none of the angels who look human (at least mostly) have the Mortal Mask Numina implies that it's not the case. If so, why does the Mortal Mask Numina exist? For those things that normally look inhuman but might switch forms?<br /> <br /> 5) Do exiles usually have Infrastructure they can materialize at, or do they find some sort of way to exist in such a way as to interact with the Unchained?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T23:10:18-08:00","id":15169,"title":"","content":"Wilderness - because if you do attract attention when you're in a crowd, the angels that turn up still have to find you <i>in</i> that crowd. If you attract attention with no one else around for miles, the angels are smart enough to know that even if you seem human, it was probably you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:29:51-08:00","id":15196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15135#post15135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The text under Aetheric Resonance says that angels don't have any counterpart for flushing out the Unchained. However, under Aetheric Sense in the Cryptid section it says that it's what Angels use to track down demons. Which is correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means Angels will sometimes deliberately breed Cryptids that can sense Aether, and use them as bloodhounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:47:17-08:00","id":15210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15196#post15196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means Angels will sometimes deliberately breed Cryptids that can sense Aether, and use them as bloodhounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, that was a heck of a misread on my part. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T01:26:52-08:00","id":15228,"title":"","content":"Got also a question (writing on phone so prob. many typing etrrors) Is a reverse soul pact possible? example the demon cant take it no more but also diesnt want the gm to win in the end by his destruction. so he decides to give all that he was and is to a human and get annihilated himself (thus soulpact with the demon being destroyed instead of the human)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T01:32:07-08:00","id":15235,"title":"","content":"Nothing in the books supports it, but it sounds like an interesting story to bring up to your ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T02:42:48-08:00","id":15273,"title":"","content":"iam the st that idea was brought up to i saw that nothing in the book supports that but then again also nothing concrete atanding against it. so i asked myself if that is going against the fluff. but wasnt sure thus asked above (one thing that i SEE as \u00fcossible problem rulewise is having starting embeds/exploits as the memories of the demon would not be transferred on a soulpact) on that not a 2. question also. is it possible to transfer memories of events or memories of skills to a cover as part of a mormal pact ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T08:19:39-08:00","id":15393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15055#post15055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to spend time in a Cover to keep it from degrading, but if you made a pact for someone's office job, you need to show up for it or you'll probably get fired. Getting fired, though, doesn't affect your cover rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. See, that is directly against my reading of Cover, and that of my players. We were all under the impression you did in fact have to spend time maintaining your Cover by doing stuff the Cover would do, because <i>not </i>doing it would count as a Compromise because it's out of character.<br /> <br /> Reference: Age and Injury, page 274","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":".  found my references, thanks to one of my players 11-21-2013, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T10:20:57-08:00","id":15459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15393#post15393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. See, that is directly against my reading of Cover, and that of my players. We were all under the impression you did in fact have to spend time maintaining your Cover by doing stuff the Cover would do, because <i>not </i>doing it would count as a Compromise because it's out of character.<br /> <br /> Reference: Age and Injury, page 274</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I was unclear: I was saying there's not a direct relationship between <i>time </i>and Cover, but you're right that you do have to maintain the identity some. For example: we're talking about my Cover, Sean the accountant. Sean could plausibly not show up for work for a week, then get fired, but still be Sean, because I've kept up with other Sean-related stuff like calling the mother I bought once a week. So Sean losing his job is a thing about Sean that can change and evolve without making me seem like not-Sean.<br /> <br /> Now, how much Sean-related stuff do I have to do to plausibly be Sean? That's a fuzzy line, and depends a lot on how your chronicle is structured. You might be playing a game where the demons are investigating things primarily &quot;after hours&quot; and we don't see much of what they do in Cover. Or you might be playing a game where a big part of the story is dealing with your relationships with humans, in which case disappearing randomly and not making your commitments is &quot;grossly out of character&quot; and the resulting compromises are a big worry. Or you might be playing a thriller where one particular aspect of a Cover takes center stage -- say you bought a teenage son and now you have 24 hours to rescue him from kidnappers, and <i>not</i> doing so would be a violation of your Cover as a previously loving parent.<br /> <br /> There will be more talk about nuances in the Player's Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T10:36:30-08:00","id":15470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15077#post15077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there intended to be a sort of fuzzy idea of a point at which an external merit granted in a Soul Pact becomes 'owned' by the target and is thus harvestable into the cover based on them? Or is 'don't sell someone something you'll need' part of the idea of Soul Pact crafting, instead reserving rewards for the clever demon who sells a mark abilities that will make them predisposed to acquire what the demon wants in their eventual cover?<br /> <br /> ...I actually find myself rather favoring the second option now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I don't quite understand the question. If you're saying &quot;would it be a good idea to help someone cultivate the life your character wants to live,&quot; then yes, it would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15077#post15077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For clarity: Does this confirm that if a Cover (or !God help the Demon, multiple covers) has a full-time job or other heavily time-obligated situation, the Cover is required to fully act that out and the partial stasis of not being the active cover only applies to internal aspects? So a Cover with, say, a job as an ER doctor can't feasibly share a Demon with a police officer or cubicle farmer? (Or at least, not remain all of them).</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to act out your Covers, yes. There isn't a specific rule on how they share time, but there isn't an effect that covers for you not doing the things associated with your Cover. Covers <i>can</i> evolve some without triggering compromise rolls, but in general if you have a Cover and then forget all about that person it's going to compromise you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15077#post15077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds legit. Having extraneous, non-supernaturally-enforced terms in the document carrying the pact doesn't interfere with it, though? Or does the mystical machinery the demon uses to quick-author a pact get cranky like my home network printer when a demon tries to pull that?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHonestly, I wouldn't let my players slip in extra provisions that don't relate to the contract. Obviously, they can put in language that obfuscates and weasels around the core of the pact, but I'd find putting mundane clauses in to involve too much additional information tracking from a Storyteller perspective. I'd call that Storyteller discretion, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T12:40:27-08:00","id":15537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15470#post15470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm sorry, I don't quite understand the question. If you're saying &quot;would it be a good idea to help someone cultivate the life your character wants to live,&quot; then yes, it would.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah that question was a mess, sorry. I meant to ask if there was intended to be any sort of snap-back built in against directly showering a mortal with Cover-applicable merits in a Soul Pact and then taking their life as soon as they kick in, to take advantage of those merits through the resulting Cover. ... hopefully that's less muddled but I'm not sure. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15470#post15470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to act out your Covers, yes. There isn't a specific rule on how they share time, but there isn't an effect that covers for you not doing the things associated with your Cover. Covers can evolve some without triggering compromise rolls, but in general if you have a Cover and then forget all about that person it's going to compromise you.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks for the clarification. I'm glad the logistical concerns of Covers don't get glossed over. There are a lot of tough choices to be made there, especially if a Demon gets really attached to an increasingly inconvenient Cover's life. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15470#post15470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHonestly, I wouldn't let my players slip in extra provisions that don't relate to the contract. Obviously, they can put in language that obfuscates and weasels around the core of the pact, but I'd find putting mundane clauses in to involve too much additional information tracking from a Storyteller perspective. I'd call that Storyteller discretion, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Makes sense. I can see it as being against the spirit of the process, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:00:32-08:00","id":15610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15537#post15537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah that question was a mess, sorry. I meant to ask if there was intended to be any sort of snap-back built in against directly showering a mortal with Cover-applicable merits in a Soul Pact and then taking their life as soon as they kick in, to take advantage of those merits through the resulting Cover. ... hopefully that's less muddled but I'm not sure. Thanks for the clarification. I'm glad the logistical concerns of Covers don't get glossed over. There are a lot of tough choices to be made there, especially if a Demon gets really attached to an increasingly inconvenient Cover's life. Makes sense. I can see it as being against the spirit of the process, too.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, in other words, if someone were to make a pact wherein they trade their soul in exchange for, say, beauty (striking looks) and then the demon cashes in on the deal, does the demon gain that beauty (the merit) when using that cover? It would make sense, since the trait bargained for becomes an inherent physical quality of the person being subsumed. The thing is, that makes the deal all upside for the demon. Sure, I'll give you wealth, beauty, fame, power, adoration, talent, and whatever the heck else you want. I'm going to BECOME you anyway, so I'm really just giving myself a bunch of free merits here. And since an unbalanced contract only costs extra willpower if its unbalanced in my favor, may as well load your end of the deal up as much as possible. This also makes it easier to tempt people, since the sweeter you make the deal for them, the more benefits you'll gain when you take their place. You want to trade your soul to become the president of the United States? Gladly! Better practice my public speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:39:04-08:00","id":15737,"title":"","content":"Aye. Sometimes limits have to be put in just to make it easier for the ST to put the brakes on a player who will otherwise find and exploit all these things.<br /> <br /> (Which would be very Demon-appropriate, but my tablemates are all human as far as i know. ...*peers*)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:50:47-08:00","id":15746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15737#post15737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye. Sometimes limits have to be put in just to make it easier for the ST to put the brakes on a player who will otherwise find and exploit all these things. (Which would be very Demon-appropriate, but my tablemates are all human as far as i know. ...*peers*)</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the default solution is that a.) most, if not all people demon PCs will be making pacts with will be NPCs, so the ST is in control of what that person wants and will or will not sell their soul for, and b.) big deals require significant redirection of resources (English definition, not merit) and a decent amount of rewriting reality. It will therefore attract quite a but of god machine attention. If players get out of hand with a pact, the ST has the power to call for compromise rolls and/or impose conditions, or what ever else feels appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T18:42:06-08:00","id":15776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15746#post15746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the default solution is that a.) most, if not all people demon PCs will be making pacts with will be NPCs, so the ST is in control of what that person wants and will or will not sell their soul for, and b.) big deals require significant redirection of resources (English definition, not merit) and a decent amount of rewriting reality. It will therefore attract quite a but of god machine attention. If players get out of hand with a pact, the ST has the power to call for compromise rolls and/or impose conditions, or what ever else feels appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but that's the ST having to patch things up. It's always less hassle to houserule and spot-rule boosts and leeway to players than drawbacks and restrictions. Not everyone has the luxury of entirely reasonable players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T20:19:09-08:00","id":15823,"title":"","content":"I thought the book said that Covers didn't grant merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T20:29:31-08:00","id":15830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15823#post15823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the book said that Covers didn't grant merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't, but see Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T20:44:22-08:00","id":15847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15823#post15823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the book said that Covers didn't grant merits?</div> </div> </div> </div> They don't, but it can get a bit narratively wonky when someone gives up their soul to be beautiful, and then as soon as the demon enters your body it just... Stops being as pretty...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T21:26:23-08:00","id":15864,"title":"","content":"Given that Embeds are physical laws that exist in nature, can anyone other than Demons make use of them? Can a Demon teach a human (or other supernatural being) how to use an Embed? If not, why?<br /> <br /> I mean, if a Demon tried to teach a human a given Embed, which would it be like?<br /> a) Teaching a child to ride a bike, where, after some some practice, handholding, and falls, the human would be able to pull it off pretty well?<br /> b) Trying to explain how to ride a bike over the phone, in Russian, to someone who only speaks English, so it's just a bunch of meaningless noises?<br /> c) Trying to teach a dolphin to ride a bike? I.e. regardless of how intelligent and capable the dolphin may or may not be at understanding your explaination of how riding a bike works, they're simply not physically capable of manipulating the bike in the first place, so the attempt is doomed to fail.<br /> d) Trying to teach a snail to ride a bike, where the whole idea is just pointless?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T22:12:16-08:00","id":15885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15830#post15830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't, but see Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And even 'hard' external merits like Resources need knowing bank PINs and brokerage account numbers to access properly, or a Library isn't very useful until you familiarize yourself with it, so relying on Legend in a newly stolen identity to access what they once had (until Merit dots and skills catch up to the important bits) is pretty natural. A mortal with a lot more going for them than the average Joe is going to have more uses of Legend fit well, and stepping into a ridiculously-Pactbuffed-mortal feels hollow compared to having to Faust up the already rich &amp; powerful or cultivate someone with more effort. Eh. Overall, it's a small concern. I love Cover anyway.<br /> <br /> edit: Really should have quoted what I was responding to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 11-22-2013, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T22:25:16-08:00","id":15890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15864#post15864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Embeds are physical laws that exist in nature, can anyone other than Demons make use of them? Can a Demon teach a human (or other supernatural being) how to use an Embed? If not, why? I mean, if a Demon tried to teach a human a given Embed, which would it be like? a) Teaching a child to ride a bike, where, after some some practice, handholding, and falls, the human would be able to pull it off pretty well? b) Trying to explain how to ride a bike over the phone, in Russian, to someone who only speaks English, so it's just a bunch of meaningless noises? c) Trying to teach a dolphin to ride a bike? I.e. regardless of how intelligent and capable the dolphin may or may not be at understanding your explaination of how riding a bike works, they're simply not physically capable of manipulating the bike in the first place, so the attempt is doomed to fail. d) Trying to teach a snail to ride a bike, where the whole idea is just pointless?</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering the half-human children of demons are specifically stated to be able to learn Embeds, the implication would seem to be that is not something normal humans are able to do. So I would guess option c, but if a or b suits your story better, there's no real reason you couldn't use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T22:59:19-08:00","id":15907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15847#post15847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They don't, but it can get a bit narratively wonky when someone gives up their soul to be beautiful, and then as soon as the demon enters your body it just... Stops being as pretty...</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but, as a number of people have pointed out upthread, if Covers could grant Merits, then a Soul Pact where the human gets Resources, Striking Looks, Staff, Allies, and as many other social merits as you want to add on has pretty much no downside for the demon, since they'll be the one getting those benefits in about five minutes. Admittedly, it does require you to erase a human from existence, which should be a horrific downside, but anyone willing to game the system to a serious degree probably won't care about that.<br /> <br /> So, balance-wise, I get why Covers don't grant Merits. That said, if it wasn't going to impact a given group's enjoyment (i.e. they either just want to increase verisimilitude to improve the play experience or they don't mind if everyone has Social Merits out the wazoo and/or finding ways in play to game the system like that are what everyone likes), then I think having it so Pacts can transfer Merits too would be a fine house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T23:00:40-08:00","id":15910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15847#post15847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They don't, but it can get a bit narratively wonky when someone gives up their soul to be beautiful, and then as soon as the demon enters your body it just... Stops being as pretty...</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept of 'Hollywood ugly' may apply. However, yeah; it's a continuity issue. Still, people can let themselves go (though doing it too suddenly might be a Cover issue), and then recover... tabloids would go out of business*, otherwise.<br /> <br /> *Well, they'd still probably be avenues of supplemental employment for fiction authors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T23:45:35-08:00","id":15923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15907#post15907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Agreed, but, as a number of people have pointed out upthread, if Covers could grant Merits, then a Soul Pact where the human gets Resources, Striking Looks, Staff, Allies, and as many other social merits as you want to add on has pretty much no downside for the demon, since they'll be the one getting those benefits in about five minutes. Admittedly, it does require you to erase a human from existence, which should be a horrific downside, but anyone willing to game the system to a serious degree probably won't care about that. So, balance-wise, I get why Covers don't grant Merits. That said, if it wasn't going to impact a given group's enjoyment (i.e. they either just want to increase verisimilitude to improve the play experience or they don't mind if everyone has Social Merits out the wazoo and/or finding ways in play to game the system like that are what everyone likes), then I think having it so Pacts can transfer Merits too would be a fine house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. To me the mechanical imbalance outweighs the potential dissonance issues, but for others it may be the other way around, and for those people I see no reason they shouldn't play it as they prefer, so long as they understand and accept the mechanical implications (you'll notice if was the guy pointing out the all-upside nature of soul pacts when run that way.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T01:00:52-08:00","id":15959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15910#post15910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The concept of 'Hollywood ugly' may apply. However, yeah; it's a continuity issue. Still, people can let themselves go (though doing it too suddenly might be a Cover issue), and then recover... tabloids would go out of business*, otherwise.<br /> <br /> *Well, they'd still probably be avenues of supplemental employment for fiction authors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I don't think it'd be too much more of a continuity issue than, say, taking over someone's job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:52:20-08:00","id":16210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=15959#post15959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I dunno, I don't think it'd be too much more of a continuity issue than, say, taking over someone's job.</div> </div> </div> </div> In a Soul Pact, taking over someone's job is continuous with becoming them. Taking someone's job as part of a normal pact has some dangers depending on how far the reach of 'directly affected' is in that case (I think Rose or Matt clarified that is fairly broad but I can't find where). There are a scant few Merits that deal explicitly with someone's outward appearance - striking looks is the only one I can recall offhand - which is somewhat trickier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T13:03:21-08:00","id":16244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=16210#post16210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In a Soul Pact, taking over someone's job is continuous with becoming them. Taking someone's job as part of a normal pact has some dangers depending on how far the reach of 'directly affected' is in that case (I think Rose or Matt clarified that is fairly broad but I can't find where). There are a scant few Merits that deal explicitly with someone's outward appearance - striking looks is the only one I can recall offhand - which is somewhat trickier.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not just appearance though, it's anything directly related to the physical body the demon inhabits. For example, giant size. If someone wished to be the tallest man on earth as part of a soul pact, it would be pretty weird for him to shrink back to normal size when the demon calls in the soul and takes over his giant body. Other examples could include small frame, fleet of foot (though that one is arguable), etc. It's just kind of odd when an inherent physical quality of a body just goes away when the demon takes control of it. My solution will probably be to allow the demon to keep the description, but lose the associated mechanical benefits until they buy the appropriate merit, or else let the player go into XP debt for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T20:20:02-08:00","id":16440,"title":"","content":"i would imagine that the appearance wouldn't change, but the mechanical benefits wouldn't transfer. a man who wanted to be huge would still be huge, but the hollowed out soul doesn't provide extra health. the person is still beautiful, but they can't carry the body or attitude to make them Striking enough for bonuses. you may have a great job, but you can't yet access the wealth. the &quot;code&quot; that determines what capabilities the mortal had (ie his merits) was destroyed with the soul (or, it WAS the soul), and the demon poured his own codes inside. they don't always connect logically (ie why a giant guy doesnt get the merit benefits of giant), but thats part of the strange horror of demons living in a world that is basically the Matrix--the god machine's rules control the world, and hacking said world doesn't always work completely or even logically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T21:56:28-08:00","id":16461,"title":"","content":"Yay more questions!<br /> <br /> So with the exploit Ephemeral Cover, a Demon can attack ghosts and spirits and make a new cover out of them.<br /> <br /> Now I'm probably missing something, but can Demons even see ghosts and spirits? Would Blindsense or maybe Aura Sight let a Demon see a ghost or spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T01:12:32-08:00","id":16517,"title":"","content":"not unless they've manifested, no. you could very easily create a new Demonic Form power for a psychopomp of &quot;can see ghosts in twilight&quot;, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T16:09:54-08:00","id":16852,"title":"","content":"External Merits are tied to Cover. The idea that they will just go away without Legend is idiotic. When you are a multimillionaire, it's going to take a lot more to prevent you from accessing your money than a missing PIN (which you should know with a Soul Pact because you BECOME them; otherwise the Cover is useless as you won't be able to maintain it at all). The drawback is that Cover is fragile, subject to being blown, traded, lost or burned. Yeah, I'm rich and influential...until I have to burn my Cover. Then it all goes away in noise and fire.<br /> <br /> There is no good in game reason for it. So hang it. You make someone a millionaire and take their soul, which they have to agree to by the way, then yes, you are now rich, until your Cover fails apart.<br /> <br /> Legend is for things like Fighting Style Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T16:34:40-08:00","id":16862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=16852#post16852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you are a multimillionaire, it's going to take a lot more to prevent you from accessing your money than a missing PIN (which you should know with a Soul Pact because you BECOME them; otherwise the Cover is useless as you won't be able to maintain it at all).</div> </div> </div> </div>This logic is a bit of a slippery slope because if you're not careful you find yourself at &quot;you should know everything about them inside and out, otherwise you risk compromise,&quot; which while an interesting idea, isn't the intent of the text at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T18:17:22-08:00","id":16889,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the intent in the text is &quot;Once you get the soul pact, you ahve their body and their life... but you only know as much as you did when you called in the deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T19:59:54-08:00","id":16904,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain to me why detaching yourself from a piece of Infrastructure you've jacked into to regain Aether is a Wits + Crafts roll?<br /> <br /> It seems a little, well, random. Plus it kinda makes Crafts a more &quot;weighted&quot; skill for Demons. I mean some character concepts just really don't involve Crafts. <br /> <br /> Surely something like Intelligence+Wits would be more appropriate? Representing the Demons ability to process the Infrastructures input and process it in a useful way (regaining Aether).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T20:38:11-08:00","id":16917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=16904#post16904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain to me why detaching yourself from a piece of Infrastructure you've jacked into to regain Aether is a Wits + Crafts roll?<br /> <br /> It seems a little, well, random. Plus it kinda makes Crafts a more &quot;weighted&quot; skill for Demons. I mean some character concepts just really don't involve Crafts.<br /> <br /> Surely something like Intelligence+Wits would be more appropriate? Representing the Demons ability to process the Infrastructures input and process it in a useful way (regaining Aether).</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels are Mechanical beings, Craft is tied to the whole Techgnostic/Godmachine vibe, it fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T23:26:45-08:00","id":16965,"title":"","content":"Today's random questions: Force Relationship, one of my new favorite Exploits. Does the -3 penalty stack with multiple uses of this Exploit? How about with the -3 you get for having a soul pact or patchwork pact above 5?<br /> <br /> When a demon spends Cover xp to raise it and solidify the relationship, does the -3 penalty stick around? By a strict reading it does, but I'm not so sure that's a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T05:01:12-08:00","id":17078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=16917#post16917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels are Mechanical beings, Craft is tied to the whole Techgnostic/Godmachine vibe, it fits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...not buying that. The God Machine deals with Occult Physics just as much as it deal with &quot;mundane&quot; physics. While I appreciate that an ST and empathize the &quot;gears and pulleys&quot; aspect. I don't t see why that interpretation needs to be made predominate in a section of the rules when its not anywhere else in the book.<br /> <br /> Angels are bio-synthetic hybrids forged using mundane and occult methods unknown and undreamed of by man. To try to use Crafts to represent the integration of a Demon into Infrastructure is a little to &quot;base&quot; for me.<br /> <br /> It's just weird. A demon that knows how to fix a clock radio (Crafts 1) is better then the demon who has spent time analyzing the demonic state (Occult 3)? Or for that matter better at attaching to Infrastructure then a demon who does not know how to fix a clock radio (no Crafts at all). <br /> <br /> Really using a skill at all if a bit weird. I think a two Attribute pool or even Attribute + Primum/Cover could have worked. <br /> <br /> Something I'll likely homebrew in anycase. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T14:14:51-08:00","id":17301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=16862#post16862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This logic is a bit of a slippery slope because if you're not careful you find yourself at &quot;you should know everything about them inside and out, otherwise you risk compromise,&quot; which while an interesting idea, isn't the intent of the text at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>And on the flip side of that slope you suddenly are supposed to maintain a Cover without knowing you birthday, home town, mother's maiden name, possibly mother's name, your wife's birthday, possibly your wife's name, possibly if you are even married, your e-mail address, your passwords (you know a TON of passwords right now), your phone, possibly your address, quite possibly what you even do for a living. The minute anyone asks you even the most basic question about your ID it's going to fall apart. For Patchwork jobs this might be reasonable, since there was never a real person there to begin with, but for a Soul pact you should get more bang for your buck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T14:21:23-08:00","id":17303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=17301#post17301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And on the flip side of that slope you suddenly are supposed to maintain a Cover without knowing you birthday, home town, mother's maiden name, possibly mother's name, your wife's birthday, possibly your wife's name, possibly if you are even married, your e-mail address, your passwords (you know a TON of passwords right now), your phone, possibly your address, quite possibly what you even do for a living.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the flip side of that flip side is that you have a perfect memory and only need to learn these things once and will probably have gone to the trouble to do so if you've been vetting a person as a candidate for replacement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T17:29:45-08:00","id":17399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=17078#post17078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah...not buying that. The God Machine deals with Occult Physics just as much as it deal with &quot;mundane&quot; physics. While I appreciate that an ST and empathize the &quot;gears and pulleys&quot; aspect. I don't t see why that interpretation needs to be made predominate in a section of the rules when its not anywhere else in the book.<br /> <br /> Angels are bio-synthetic hybrids forged using mundane and occult methods unknown and undreamed of by man. To try to use Crafts to represent the integration of a Demon into Infrastructure is a little to &quot;base&quot; for me.<br /> <br /> It's just weird. A demon that knows how to fix a clock radio (Crafts 1) is better then the demon who has spent time analyzing the demonic state (Occult 3)? Or for that matter better at attaching to Infrastructure then a demon who does not know how to fix a clock radio (no Crafts at all).<br /> <br /> Really using a skill at all if a bit weird. I think a two Attribute pool or even Attribute + Primum/Cover could have worked.<br /> <br /> Something I'll likely homebrew in anycase.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels aren't bio-synthetic hybrids though, the only bio portion comes from Covers, Angels are Cybernetic/Clockwork beings, you use the medium of technology to apply what you know about how your body works to detach. Why is making Craft important even an issue, wouldn't replacing it with Occult be the same issue? A Demon without any Craft will therefore have blind spots about how their very body and nature works, just like how a human without Medicine will have a lot of question marks about how their body works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T17:56:54-08:00","id":17406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=17399#post17399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels aren't bio-synthetic hybrids though, the only bio portion comes from Covers, Angels are Cybernetic/Clockwork beings, you use the medium of technology to apply what you know about how your body works to detach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels and demons both run the entire bio/mechanical spectrum. The operative reason that Crafts is appropriate is because the portions of Infrastructure <i>that you can hook into</i>? are mechanical. You are literally directing waste heat into yourself at the moment and knowing how physical objects work as part of a mechanism is a Crafts trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T19:10:58-08:00","id":17446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=17303#post17303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the flip side of that flip side is that you have a perfect memory and only need to learn these things once and will probably have gone to the trouble to do so if you've been vetting a person as a candidate for replacement.</div> </div> </div> </div>So of course you have the time to scout around before and do all the important legwork to find out the details of how your target got that scar on his right hand when he was eleven, but his bank account and PIN were just too much work to bother with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T02:33:28-08:00","id":17626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14823-random-demon-questions?p=17446#post17446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So of course you have the time to scout around before and do all the important legwork to find out the details of how your target got that scar on his right hand when he was eleven, but his bank account and PIN were just too much work to bother with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't know what you are trying to say with this. Both those things are (more or less) important to stay in character in your soon to be Cover, so both should be (ideally) learned. And that's the point really, you have to learn them, you don't get any of this info as part of the Soul Pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reacti